Initial failure record, native cancellation restore validation

This is a contemporaneous transcription of the first CTest tool response from
2026-10-15. The initial command was:

LD_LIBRARY_PATH=/workspace/template/work/protobuf-root/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu:/workspace/template/work/build-native-cancel-v2/AstraSim/lib:/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu /workspace/template/work/tool-env/bin/ctest --test-dir work/build-native-cancel-v2 -R 'NativeCoarseProjectionTest|NativeProjectionCApiTest' --output-on-failure

Observed first-run result:
- NativeProjectionCApiTest passed.
- NativeCoarseProjectionTest failed at the restore-mutation assertion:
  "outer and retained Domain cancellation terminals must agree".
- All preceding new cancel assertions had passed.

Follow-up found the test mutation loop could silently fail to find the retained
restore endpoint binding. Added a mandatory `changed` assertion inside the
mutation callback so the invalid snapshot must mutate that binding. Rebuilt the
test and the same CTest command then passed 2/2.

The first output was not redirected to disk when it ran; this file preserves the
observed command and failure details rather than presenting a fabricated raw
terminal transcript.
